l":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5791,"closed_issues":0,"state":"open","created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T22:40:26Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-11T13:57:07Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T11:59:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121228","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121228","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121228.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121228.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"The threading model used by HTTPRequest and the way HTTPClient blocking mode is implemented, makes it really hard to implement efficient download loops, forcing us to rely on a very busy loop which doesn't actually block on the socket.\r\n\r\nThis is an attempt at making the HTTPClient actually block on the socket using [`shutdown`](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/shutdown.2.html) ([Win](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winsock/nf-winsock-shutdown)) to signal the downloading thread it should quit.\r\n\r\nFixes #33479\r\nFixes #35868\r\nFixes #119782\r\n\r\nCloses #117749 .\r\n\r\nSide Note\r\n--\r\n\r\nReasoning on the thread safety of this implementation is non-trivial, but relies on the following constraints:\r\n\r\n- The `tcp_connection` instance of the `HTTPClientTCP` never changes (i.e. never re-assigned after instantiation)\r\n- The underlying `NetSocket` of the `tcp_connection` never changes (i.e. never re-assigned after instantiation)\r\n- The call to `NetSocket::shutdown` thread-safe`*` (does not mutate the NetSocket state beside making the relevant socket syscall).\r\n- The `HTTPRequest` never instantiate a new `HTTPClient` from the thread.\r\n\r\n\r\n`*` There is a very scary blurb in the [MS docs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winsock/nf-winsock-shutdown) about APCs and thread safety, but if I understand the MS-speak correctly what we are doing here should be fine.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121228/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":3,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121228/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}